[["page","lines",23],{"text":"eligible women. In particular, we double-checked whether there are any imbalances between the","fontSize":10.9091,"x":70.866,"y":552.7949,"width":470.26948279999976,"height":10.909099999999967}]
[["page","lines",24],{"text":"groups, but concluded that this was not the case (as can be seen in Table IV in Appendix D).","fontSize":10.9091,"x":70.866,"y":574.7169,"width":470.2749373499994,"height":10.909099999999967}]
[["page","lines",25],{"text":"Furthermore, these results are robust to the introduction of covariates, as shown in Table V. A second","fontSize":10.9091,"x":70.866,"y":596.6399,"width":470.2673009799995,"height":10.909099999999967}]
[["page","lines",26],{"text":"possibility is that the sharp fall in screening rates reflects a higher screening rate in the control group","fontSize":10.9091,"x":70.866,"y":618.5629,"width":470.26402824999957,"height":10.909099999999967}]
[["page","lines",27],{"text":"rather than a fall in the treatment groups. In fact, the screening rate in the control group in the Eure","fontSize":10.9091,"x":70.866,"y":640.4849,"width":470.26402824999957,"height":10.909099999999967}]
[["page","lines",28],{"text":"is 60%, while that in the treatment group is close to the total sample average. We thus interpret","fontSize":10.9091,"x":70.866,"y":662.4079,"width":470.2651191599995,"height":10.909099999999967}]
[["page","lines",29],{"text":"this as a Type-I error, i.e. the null was falsely rejected. Given the number of subgroups, it is likely","fontSize":10.9091,"x":70.866,"y":684.3299,"width":470.2716646199997,"height":10.90910000000008}]
[["page","lines",30],{"text":"that this kind of Type-I error would arise for one subgroup. To further investigate, we collected","fontSize":10.9091,"x":70.866,"y":706.2529,"width":470.2705737099998,"height":10.90910000000008}]
[["page","lines",31],{"text":"16","fontSize":10.9091,"x":300.576,"y":740.1129,"width":10.848009040000022,"height":10.90910000000008}]
